@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;verification] container-image-buck2-only
The offline-analysis image MUST be built only through the Buck2 targets
`//.oss-scanner:image` (build, load and scan) and `//.oss-scanner:image-publish`
(`buck2 run`: push and scan), which buck/container_image.py drives with
`docker buildx` over this Dockerfile and the repository root, `.git` included.
The Marshall release it carries MUST be the Buck2 dependency
`//:package-service-marshall`, imported from the `release` build context;
nothing in the Dockerfile may build it. oss-scanner.yml MUST call those
targets through tools/buck2, never a Docker build action or `docker build`
directly, and MUST push only from trunk. The targets MUST stay non_hermetic,
Linux-only, local_only and uncached, so `buck2 build //...`, verification and
tools/affected skip them (ADR-0269). The context's `.git` MUST be
self-contained (no objects/info/alternates).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;build] container-image-no-token
No Namespace token may enter any image layer, the image configuration or a
build context. docker MUST receive no token as a build argument, secret or
environment variable (the driver drops NAMESPACE_RBE_TOKEN), no Buck2 may run
inside the image build, and the repository context MUST exclude the
checkout's Buck2 state (Dockerfile.dockerignore). Both targets MUST stream
every member of the built or published image, decompressed, through the
token scan and fail on any token-shaped string (`nsrt_` and at least 20 token
characters; a bare mention of the prefix in documentation is not one),
printing member names only (ADR-0276).
